WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.580 --> 00:00:05.290
. Continuing with unsurprising corona virus
news.

00:00:05.290 --> 00:00:10.870
Schools of all kinds of started to open elementary,
middle high school colleges and universities

00:00:10.870 --> 00:00:13.190
and corona virus clusters are exploding now.

00:00:13.190 --> 00:00:17.580
I wish I could say, you know, it really seemed
like this wasn't going to happen.

00:00:17.580 --> 00:00:18.590
We're shocked by this.

00:00:18.590 --> 00:00:21.119
This was it was just unpredictable.

00:00:21.119 --> 00:00:22.529
We knew that this was going to happen.

00:00:22.529 --> 00:00:27.340
A few stories from around the country at Purdue
University.

00:00:27.340 --> 00:00:33.850
Cases, student cases on campus are already
at 41 within just a few days of students moving

00:00:33.850 --> 00:00:34.850
in.

00:00:34.850 --> 00:00:36.960
Remember that it often takes five days to
show symptoms.

00:00:36.960 --> 00:00:41.680
So certainly it's more than 41 cases that
will ultimately be discovered at Purdue Universities

00:00:41.680 --> 00:00:42.680
campus.

00:00:42.680 --> 00:00:47.610
In Florida, nearly 9000 kids have tested positive
in the two weeks since schools reopened.

00:00:47.610 --> 00:00:52.340
That brings the total number of cases in Florida
among those under 18 to close to 50000 cases.

00:00:52.340 --> 00:01:01.080
If you look across the country, you have about
750 colleges and universities now with cases.

00:01:01.080 --> 00:01:02.980
University of North Carolina is a bad one.

00:01:02.980 --> 00:01:07.680
They've had to send most undergraduate students
home already.

00:01:07.680 --> 00:01:09.650
It's not even September.

00:01:09.650 --> 00:01:15.090
North Carolina had so many cases in the dorms
that most undergrads have already been sent

00:01:15.090 --> 00:01:16.090
home.

00:01:16.090 --> 00:01:20.360
Notre Dame is delaying classes because dozens
of students have tested positive there.

00:01:20.360 --> 00:01:23.410
Iowa State, dozens of cases in the dorms.

00:01:23.410 --> 00:01:28.610
One of the worst outbreaks is at the University
of Alabama at Birmingham, where there are

00:01:28.610 --> 00:01:31.180
nearly a thousand cases.

00:01:31.180 --> 00:01:34.020
University of Central Florida, 750 cases.

00:01:34.020 --> 00:01:36.650
I'm not going to give you the whole list,
but it's everywhere.

00:01:36.650 --> 00:01:38.450
And it was completely predictable.

00:01:38.450 --> 00:01:42.940
Now, I want to remind everybody in the audience,
because every time I talk about this, I get

00:01:42.940 --> 00:01:45.160
the same confused emails.

00:01:45.160 --> 00:01:49.540
I am not pretending, especially when it comes
to school age, kids, elementary, middle school,

00:01:49.540 --> 00:01:52.360
high school, that this is a simple issue.

00:01:52.360 --> 00:01:53.700
This is not a simple issue.

00:01:53.700 --> 00:01:57.090
You have parents who can't work if their kids
aren't in school.

00:01:57.090 --> 00:02:02.540
You have parents that have jobs that you can't
work from home, but they don't pay enough

00:02:02.540 --> 00:02:08.519
to pay for childcare, meaning it wouldn't
make sense if their kids are at home to go

00:02:08.519 --> 00:02:10.399
to work and pay for childcare.

00:02:10.399 --> 00:02:11.410
They just can't work.

00:02:11.410 --> 00:02:13.230
They've got to stay home.

00:02:13.230 --> 00:02:16.320
That's a systemic problem with the country.

00:02:16.320 --> 00:02:21.020
We've not done enough in terms of stimulus
compared to other countries.

00:02:21.020 --> 00:02:24.959
It is a complicated situation, but it is a
systemic problem.

00:02:24.959 --> 00:02:29.080
You, of course, have parents who just insist
this is no big deal and want to send their

00:02:29.080 --> 00:02:30.830
kids to school.

00:02:30.830 --> 00:02:34.270
You have parents who believe, you know, corona
virus conspiracy theories.

00:02:34.270 --> 00:02:36.090
You have all that stuff.

00:02:36.090 --> 00:02:41.360
But the real problem is not so much parents
choosing to send their kids to school because

00:02:41.360 --> 00:02:43.460
they're not worried about the virus.

00:02:43.460 --> 00:02:50.020
This is really a systemic problem that has
put a lot of parents into untenable situations.

00:02:50.020 --> 00:02:53.569
Now, that's different than colleges and universities.

00:02:53.569 --> 00:02:57.810
We're talking about if things go correctly,
you just need to do remote learning in the

00:02:57.810 --> 00:02:58.840
fall.

00:02:58.840 --> 00:03:02.670
Clearly, this fall semester should be done
remote.

00:03:02.670 --> 00:03:03.870
It should be done online.

00:03:03.870 --> 00:03:05.240
It should have been done from day one.

00:03:05.240 --> 00:03:06.260
Some schools did it.

00:03:06.260 --> 00:03:07.950
Others have refused to do it.

00:03:07.950 --> 00:03:09.770
We're not talking about forever.

00:03:09.770 --> 00:03:14.760
And I get that if you're an incoming freshman,
this is not a fun way to start college.

00:03:14.760 --> 00:03:17.400
This is probably not even the best way to
start college.

00:03:17.400 --> 00:03:20.330
From the perspective of learning, I get it.

00:03:20.330 --> 00:03:26.250
But let's not miss the forest for the trees
having to shut down a semester in progress

00:03:26.250 --> 00:03:31.390
and send people home sometimes days after
the semester started.

00:03:31.390 --> 00:03:35.060
It's way more disruptive than just saying,
hey, guys, you know, it sucks, but we're going

00:03:35.060 --> 00:03:36.230
to do remote for the fall.

00:03:36.230 --> 00:03:43.190
And then hopefully in the spring we can start
to go back to normal, spending the time developing

00:03:43.190 --> 00:03:48.080
a good remote learning system for the fall
rather than bringing students in endless testing

00:03:48.080 --> 00:03:50.270
cases pop up sending students home.

00:03:50.270 --> 00:03:52.140
It would have made far more sense.

00:03:52.140 --> 00:03:54.450
Elementary, middle, high school.

00:03:54.450 --> 00:03:56.650
I'm not pretending it isn't complicated.

00:03:56.650 --> 00:04:00.410
The problems are more systemic than they are
individual.

00:04:00.410 --> 00:05:14.969
Our federal government has failed quite simply.

